The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series. '''StarCraft II''' was announced as part of the line-up on February 2, 2024.<ref name="EWC SC2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESWCgg/status/1753448233043419375|title=The world's most storied esport is joining the official #EsportsWorldCup lineup!|date=2024-02-02|author=Esports World Cup|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>

==Format==
*'''Main Stage''':
**16 players into 2 Groups of 8 players each.
***Double-elimination brackets.
***All matches are {{abbr/Bo5}}.
****Winner of each group advances to the Final Four.
****2nd Place of each group play a match, Winner advances to the Final Four.
*'''Knockout Bracket''':
**13 players from the Main Stage and 2 players from the Qualifiers.
***Single-elimination bracket.
***All matches are {{abbr/Bo3}}.
***Finals are {{abbr/Bo5}}.
****Winner advances to the Final Four.
*'''Final Four''':
**Single-elimination bracket.
***Semifinals are {{abbr/Bo7}}.
***Grand Finals are {{abbr/Bo9}}.

